# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment files
#
# Everything matching .env* is ignored, then the templates are allowed back by
# name. The order matters: a later rule wins, so the exceptions must follow the
# blanket rule.
#
# This file used to carry `!.env.production` under the comment "Allow production
# env vars for Vercel". Vercel does not read a committed .env file — only the
# environment variables set in its own dashboard — so the exception bought
# nothing and cost a real CLERK_SECRET_KEY, committed in plaintext in 7cad53ac
# and still present in HEAD until it was untracked.
#
# A new .env file is ignored by default. Add an exception only for a file that
# holds placeholders, never a value.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env*

# Templates — placeholders only, no real values
!.env.clerk.example
!.env.docker.dev
!.env.docker.prod
mobile-shots/
